    pr_ref:  # 5493
    description: "WHAT. A node id is language:path:lines:name:kind. Two real, different nodes with one name and one kind on one line get one id, and an edge cannot tell them apart. The validator check node_id_uniqueness (new, an error) reports each. Measured over 42 trees after the id fixes: 3 ids are still held by more than one node.\n- Swift: vapor Sources/Vapor/Content/PlaintextEncoder.swift:91, \"init() {}; init() where K == BasicCodingKey {}\": two initializers, id swift:...:91-91:FailureEncoder.init:constructor.\n- Nix: servant flake.nix:80, \"tutorial = mkDevShell { tutorial = true; };\": the outer binding and the inner attribute, id nix:flake.nix:80-80:tutorial:binding (their stable ids differ through the attribute chain).\n- Vue: \"<span v-if=\\\"a\\\"></span><span v-if=\\\"b\\\"></span>\" on one line (fixture in packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_node_id_uniqueness_check.py; 0 on koel, pretix and workadventure).\n- C: zstd lib/compress/zstd_opt.c:878-895: three macro invocations before a #define are read as three function nodes at one span with one name (ZSTD_BT_GET_ALL_MATCHES_FN). This one is a misparse, not a column question: the C analyzer should emit one node or none.\nOWNER QUESTION. JavaScript anonymous callbacks solve the same problem by writing @<column> into the id's name slot, which breaks ADR-0036 Ruling 1 (WI-bafaz, the one declared name-slot hole). Either the grammar gets a place for a column or an ordinal (then WI-bafaz and these three share one fix), or same-line twins are qualified in their NAME (Nix: the attribute chain; that renames every Nix binding). Related: WI-jigov (an edge locates to a line, not a column).\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/idfive_11232026/ (STATUS.md, <package>/RESULTS.md, bump/report_run2.txt). Found 2026-11-23 while building WI-funip, WI-supar, WI-sagur, WI-jozih and WI-sidus."  # 5493
    fields: {}  # 5493
- op: discuss  # 1a93
  at: '2026-11-23T23:19:19Z'  # 1a93
  by: agent  # 1a93
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 1a93
  clock: 2  # 1a93
  nonce: 1a93  # 1a93
  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-11-23 (in session, asked in plain terms): \"Bless the @<column> suffix.\" ADR-0036 is to be amended so that the id's name slot may carry an @<column> suffix that Symbol.name lacks, and same-line twins in other languages (Swift, Nix, Vue here) use it. No new id field; names are not qualified. This rules WI-bafaz too. The C case (zstd macro invocations read as three functions) is a parser defect and needs no ruling. Status moves to todo_hard: ruled, to build."  # 1a93
